# Cerebellum environment. Copy to cere.env next to service_ctl.sh, chmod 0600,
# and fill in the blanks. It holds a bearer token and a cloud API key: never
# commit it, never print it into a transcript.
#
# Every key in the Listener, Voice presence, Upstream and Mouth sections is
# REQUIRED and none has a default. Two exceptions: the TLS pair is optional as a
# pair, and DASHSCOPE_API_KEY may equally come from the duoduo dotenv file or the
# workspace config. That is deliberate. These values decide barge-in latency, which model answers, and
# whether room audio leaves the machine encrypted; a plausible-looking constant
# invented by the code would ferment into "the value" without anyone deciding it.
# A missing key is a hard refusal at boot, naming what to set.

# ── Listener ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bind address. Wildcards (0.0.0.0, ::, *, empty) are REFUSED: this socket
# carries continuous room audio, and a deployment machine usually has a public
# interface. Name the private-network address the channel reaches, or 127.0.0.1
# when the channel runs on this same machine.
CEREBELLUM_HOST=
CEREBELLUM_PORT=30077
# Bearer token the channel must present. Required on a private network too.
# User-provided: generate a long random string, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.
CEREBELLUM_TOKEN=
# WebSocket heartbeat period in ms. A half-open TCP connection is otherwise
# undetectable. 15000 matches the channel's own heartbeat_ms; the two are one
# convention declared twice, so change them together.
CEREBELLUM_HEARTBEAT_MS=15000

# TLS certificate and private key PATHS. Optional AS A PAIR: both present means
# wss://, both absent means plaintext ws:// for loopback debugging only, and
# exactly one present is refused at boot. The channel rejects any non-wss URL
# that is not loopback, so on a real deployment these are effectively required.
# User-provided; see README.md for minting them.
CEREBELLUM_TLS_CERT=
CEREBELLUM_TLS_KEY=

# ── Voice presence (Silero) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Path to the Silero artifact shipped at packages/cerebellum/artifacts/silero-vad.onnx.
# Its SHA-256 is verified on every load and a mismatch is fatal: nothing is
# downloaded at runtime. Absent means this machine has no voice detector, and
# there is nothing to fall back to - the energy detector was deleted, not
# disabled.
CEREBELLUM_SILERO_MODEL=/opt/ambient/cerebellum/packages/cerebellum/artifacts/silero-vad.onnx
# The three numbers below are ONE operating point, and it is PROVISIONAL: these
# are the upstream vendor's shipped values, adopted as a starting point. They are
# not a tuned calibration and no labelled curve has been measured against this
# room type. Treat a change as an experiment with a result, not as a tweak.
#
# Speech probability at or above which a hop opens a voice candidate.
CEREBELLUM_VOICE_THRESHOLD=0.5
# Hysteresis below the onset threshold: a hop counts as silence under
# (threshold - offset).
CEREBELLUM_VOICE_NEG_THRESHOLD_OFFSET=0.15
# A candidate shorter than this many ms is rejected before it reaches the ear.
# This is the knob that trades futile transcription calls against missed short
# backchannels.
CEREBELLUM_VOICE_MIN_SPEECH_MS=250

# ── Upstream services, models and state ─────────────────────────────────────
# Transcription + diarization, the FULL route. One call returns both the text and
# the speaker split, and there is no degraded path: a fallback that returned text
# without attribution would silently drop half of what the caller asked for.
AMBIENT_MOSS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:30180/v1/audio/transcriptions
# Voiceprint embedding, the FULL /embed URL. /healthz is resolved against its
# origin and its `model` field names the stored voiceprint space.
AMBIENT_SPEAKER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:30076/embed
# Understander, the FULL chat-completions URL. The client POSTs to exactly this
# string and appends no path.
AMBIENT_UNDERSTAND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:30080/v1/chat/completions
# Served model name at that endpoint. It must match what the endpoint serves
# exactly: on a mismatch the endpoint rejects the request, every judge call
# raises, and every interval settles degraded. No default, so it cannot go
# missing unnoticed.
AMBIENT_UNDERSTAND_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B-FP8
# Optional bearer credential for the understander, sent as `Authorization: Bearer`.
# Leave it empty for the loopback reference container. Set it to point the judge at
# an OpenAI-compatible API instead; docs/service-contracts.md lists the request
# fields such an endpoint must accept, and the doctrine was measured on the
# reference model only, so a different model is a measurement you run, not a swap.
#AMBIENT_UNDERSTAND_API_KEY=
# Rows of in-connection timeline kept. Not only a memory guard: it is also the
# real bound on the cold-start seed, because the channel hands over the whole
# room context on open and only the last N rows survive here. It is the judge's
# memory length after a restart.
CEREBELLUM_MAX_ROWS=500
# Persistence root for room-local anonymous speaker numbers
# (<dataDir>/speaker-voices/) and for capture orders. Without it every restart
# re-assigns "whoever speaks first is number one" and overwrites the stored
# identity.
CEREBELLUM_DATA_DIR=/opt/ambient/cerebellum/data

# ── Mouth (cloud realtime TTS) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Endpoint, model and voice are ONE BOUND TRIPLE. Swapping the endpoint alone
# leaves the room silent with no error, because another vendor tier accepts a
# different voice family and rejects this voice name. Move all three together.
TTS_REALTIME_URL=wss://dashscope.aliyuncs.com/api-ws/v1/realtime
TTS_MODEL=qwen3-tts-instruct-flash-realtime
TTS_VOICE=Cherry
# Cloud credential. User-provided; the process also accepts it from the duoduo
# dotenv file or a workspace config if this is empty.
DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=

# ── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Expressiveness instruction per speech kind. Omit both and the wire is
# byte-identical to not having the feature. Only the instruct tier honours them:
# a flash-tier model echoes them back and ignores them, so the acceptance test is
# that two opposite instructions actually change the audio, never that the
# response repeats the instruction.
#TTS_INSTRUCTIONS_ACK=
#TTS_INSTRUCTIONS_ANSWER=
# Debug dumps. Each writes one file per event into an existing directory: the
# exact judge request body, and the segment audio. Segment audio is unredacted
# room recording - enable it only for a named experiment, and delete the output
# when that experiment ends.
#CEREBELLUM_DUMP_UNDERSTAND_DIR=
#CEREBELLUM_DUMP_SEGMENTS_DIR=

# ── Read by nothing (kept here only so an old file is not misread) ──────────
# CEREBELLUM_SILENCE_RMS was the energy detector's threshold. That detector was
# deleted when Silero replaced it, and the key is now inert: leaving it in an env
# file changes nothing, and removing it changes nothing.
